od  health reasons for doing so but do you  need to vary the tastes so much like we  often do probably not that may be a  natural but not necessary desire what  about the presentation or the packaging  of it now you know when we think about  presentation of a dish  I'm very hip to culinary stuff because  you know I have a lot of friends who are  chefs and presentation is part of it  that leads to the pleasures of the eyes  but in many respects the kinds of  presentations that we do are not really  natural or necessary are they and  they're not the sort of thing that we  should really get upset about there's  nothing wrong with like taking some  pleasure in it but it's not something  that we should make a focus for  ourselves and do we need it served on  gold plates or by a waiter dressed in a  certain way probably not that's pretty  baseless desire what else let's think  about books now now Epicurus would  actually say you do need some books  certainly you need books about natural  philosophy you know that is what we  nowadays call cosmology and about you  know how the human body works and things  like that he thinks that's an important  part of  the good life what other kinds of books  might you not mean do you need fiction  books maybe not so much Epicurus would  probably say right they appeal the  things that aren't part of our human  nature  we're a memetic creature but they're not  really necessary and if you don't have  fiction books you probably aren't gonna  you know be really upset because of that  if you are it's because there's  something wrong you've built up certain  habits that make those desires too  strong for you and do we need our books  bound in beautiful leather binding you  know does that have anything to do with  the value of the book itself it doesn't  so you know the need to stock libraries  with these beautifully bound volumes  Epicurus would say is actually in many  respects based on groundless desire so  this is how he analyzes these these  three kinds of desire natural and  necessary natural but not necessary  neither natural nor necessary we've seen  a lot of examples and so hopefully this  helps you understand this distinction  that he's making
 

